And why doesn't he just say "I've eaten dinner"? What does
"already" add to that statement? Maybe because the natural
state is that dinner has not started yet?

{mi ba'o citka le sanmi} is closer to "I've eaten dinner".
"Already" adds something which is missing in both of them.

